.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt ACPI_DELL 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm acpi_dell
.Nd Dell Laptop Extras
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel,
place the following lines in your
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "device acpi_wmi"
.Cd "device acpi_dell"
.Cd "device smbios"
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, to load the driver as a
module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
acpi_dell_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides access to firmware settings of Dell laptops through the
Dell SMBIOS calling interface, which is reached over
.Xr acpi_wmi 4 .
The settings the firmware offers are discovered from the token table in the
.Xr smbios 4
data, so only the variables supported by the machine are created.
.Pp
Currently the driver supports the battery charge settings.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following sysctls are currently implemented:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va dev.acpi_dell.0.charge_mode
Battery charge mode.
One of
.Cm standard ,
.Cm express
(fast charging),
.Cm primarily_ac
(for machines that are mostly plugged in),
.Cm adaptive
(the firmware picks a mode based on usage) or
.Cm custom
(use the thresholds below).
.It Va dev.acpi_dell.0.charge_start_threshold
Battery level, in percent, below which charging starts in
.Cm custom
mode.
Valid values are 50-95 and must be at least 5 lower than
.Va charge_stop_threshold .
.It Va dev.acpi_dell.0.charge_stop_threshold
Battery level, in percent, at which charging stops in
.Cm custom
mode.
Valid values are 55-100 and must be at least 5 higher than
.Va charge_start_threshold .
.El
.Pp
The firmware stores these settings, so they persist across reboots and
also apply while the machine is powered off.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Keep the battery between 50% and 80% on a laptop that is mostly used on AC
power:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sysctl dev.acpi_dell.0.charge_mode=custom
sysctl dev.acpi_dell.0.charge_stop_threshold=80
sysctl dev.acpi_dell.0.charge_start_threshold=50
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr acpi_wmi 4 ,
.Xr smbios 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
